                <pb facs="0925" n="797" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg797"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 Pan American Airways, Inc./169:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Ecuador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bading</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-12-08T10:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 8,
                                1928—10 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>30. Pan American Airways, Incorporated, informs Department Mr. Harold E. Harris,
                    General Manager Peruvian Airways Corporation will assist Mr. Otto Berg von
                    Linde, representative of W. E. Grace and Company, to apply for operating
                    concession in Ecuador similar to concession recently granted to Scadta.</p>
                <p>Please render all possible and proper assistance. Department is much interested
                    in the development by American interests of commercial aviation service between
                    the United States and Latin America.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
